      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T17:41:19Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "This function didn\u0027t really \"initialize\" anything. Its only purpose was to make the last \"visible\" worker have the restoration buffers assigned from `AV1_COMMON` if the total number of workers changed. However, the references for the buffers that were previously dynamically generated are completely lost (and so they can no longer be free\u0027d), causing a resource lifetime issue.\n\nMaking the first worker always reuse the buffers from `AV1_COMMON` obviates doing the reassignment that this function did.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 830,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 844,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "288ad69242232a60dac6dca5697cb0154a7f39dc",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
